{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/API.md --jq .content | base64 -d | rg -n -C 2 'autoPause|bind|unpaus|pause scene|pausable'\"","aggregated_output":"94-- Adaptive size: `minW` / `minH` set the scale (the screen shows at least that many pixels), `maxW` / `maxH` cap the view (the rest is letterboxed). `portrait: { maxH: 1000 }` overrides them while the [... omitted end of long line]\n95-- `input`: `'DEFAULT'` (top-down action), `'PLATFORMER'`, `'SHMUP'`, `'THIRDPERSON'`, or your own `{ action: ['KeyQ', 'Pad0'] }`.\n96:- `views`: the views your game supports; `game.nextView()` cycles them (bind it to a key).\n97-- Start: `game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) })`, or with scenes (below).\n98-- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits;  [... omitted end of long line]\n--\n109-  title: { update(dt) { if (game.input.pressed('start')) game.go('play', { level: 1 }); },\n110-           draw(r) { r.sky(['#101848', '#402a70']); r.text('PRESS START', r.W / 2, 100, '#fff', { align: 'center', scale: 2 }); } },\n111:  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n112-          enter(data) { /* build the level */ }, exit() {}, update(dt) {}, draw(r) {} }\n113-} });\n114-```\n115:`game.go(name, data)` switches after a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`: a test advances past it; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: [... omitted end of long line]\n116-\n117-## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n--\n132-\n133-## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\n134:With no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, [... omitted end of long line]\n135:- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], contro [... omitted end of long line]\n136-- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)`  [... omitted end of long line]\n137:- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'p [... omitted end of long line]\n138-- **Boot**: heavy setup in steps behind a boot screen, and a report for any error before play: `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title, steps: [['Building the city', () => { map = build(); }]] } }) [... omitted end of long line]\n139-\n--\n145-- Players (two to four on one machine): `game.players` is `[game.input, ...]`, each an input with this API, its `player` number, `name` (`'P2'`), `color` (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and device. `game.allowJoi [... omitted end of long line]\n146-- `clear()` releases held inputs, pending presses, virtual sticks and touch buttons; focus loss does this automatically. `suppress(a)` blocks an action for the current tick; `suppressCode('Mouse0')` l [... omitted end of long line]\n147:- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down [... omitted end of long line]\n148:- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch bu [... omitted end of long line]\n149-\n150-## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n--\n290-## Before you hand the game back\n291-- One IIFE starting with `const E = My3D2dge` (between the markers in a single file; `game/game.js` in the handoff package). Only your game: no leftover starter menu or unused slices. No network, no l [... omitted end of long line]\n292:- Title screen and game-over screen as scenes; `pausable: true` on gameplay scenes. No pause, settings, rebinding or full-screen code of your own (they're standard); prompts from `game.input.label(act [... omitted end of long line]\n293-- The camera follows the player (`game.focus` every update) and shows the level; the HUD uses screen pixels, or `E.Shell`'s HTML for a modern game (the STEALTH kit; the handoff package's template).\n294-- Sound effects on jump, hit, pickup and death; music per scene.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
